# launchkey.fun — Cloudflare Pages response headers.
# Conservative by design: security headers everywhere, one-day
# caching for images/fonts only. HTML and data files keep Pages'
# defaults. No CSP (the worker-driven pages would break) and no
# HSTS (TLS policy is managed at the zone level).

# Security headers on every path.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN

# Images and fonts: cache for a day. File names are not
# content-hashed, so immutable / year-long caching would be wrong.
/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
/*.jpg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
/*.jpeg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
/*.gif
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
/*.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
/*.webp
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
/*.ico
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
/*.woff
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
/*.woff2
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
